WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
"Good morning, class" said Mr. Aron.

2
00:00:04.461 --> 00:00:08.179
"Today we have a visitor."

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.800
Jada looked up.

4
00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:20.098
The visitor was Miss Santiago, the school nurse.

5
00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:23.881
"Is somebody sick?" asked Paul.

6
00:00:23.882 --> 00:00:26.685
The nurse smiled and shook her head.

7
00:00:26.686 --> 00:00:32.230
"I'm here to talk about food allergies."

8
00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:36.027
"Ooh!" Mike waved his arm.

9
00:00:36.028 --> 00:00:40.719
"I'm allergic to peanuts!"

10
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:45.365
"I'm allergic to shrimp," said Matt.

11
00:00:45.366 --> 00:00:50.370
"I can't eat eggs," said Jennifer.

12
00:00:50.371 --> 00:00:57.031
"My sister is allergic to tree nuts," said Jada.

13
00:00:57.032 --> 00:01:03.153
"What happens if you eat these things?" asked Miss Santiago.

14
00:01:03.154 --> 00:01:08.915
"I get a bad stomachache," said Matt.

15
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:12.218
"Then I throw up!"

16
00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:21.373
"I get itchy," said Jennifer.

17
00:01:21.374 --> 00:01:26.729
"Are food allegies dangerous?" asked Carly.

18
00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:30.374
"They can be dangerous," said the nurse.

19
00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:33.948
"Some kids have severe allergies.

20
00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:36.955
Foods can stop their breathing.

21
00:01:36.956 --> 00:01:41.353
But there's medicine to help."

22
00:01:41.354 --> 00:01:43.789
Jennifer raised her hand.

23
00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:48.486
"If you're allergic to foods, what can you do?"

24
00:01:48.487 --> 00:01:52.346
"Good question, Jennifer," said Miss Santiago.

25
00:01:52.347 --> 00:01:54.457
"Anyone have an idea?

26
00:01:54.458 --> 00:01:58.473
How can you protect yourself?"

27
00:01:58.474 --> 00:02:04.098
"Always check food labels," said Carly.

28
00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:11.823
"Don't trade food with other kids," said Mike.

29
00:02:11.824 --> 00:02:17.473
"Carry your allergy medicine everywhere!" said Jada.

30
00:02:17.474 --> 00:02:21.431
"Great ideas!" said Miss Santiago.

31
00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:25.722
"You must also speak up.

32
00:02:25.723 --> 00:02:28.378
Tell teachers and friends.

33
00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:37.345
Make sure everyone knows about your allergy.

34
00:02:37.346 --> 00:02:40.487
That will keep you healthy."

35
00:02:40.488 --> 00:02:42.915
Paul raised his hand.

36
00:02:42.916 --> 00:02:45.341
"I have a severe allergy.

37
00:02:45.342 --> 00:02:50.471
But it's not a food allergy."

38
00:02:50.472 --> 00:02:54.426
"What is it then, Paul?" asked Mr. Aron.

39
00:02:54.427 --> 00:03:00.490
Paul grinned.

40
00:03:00.491 --> 00:03:08.781
"Ah-choo! I'm allergic to homework!"

